WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:07.729
Crime and Punishment; they go together like
pen and paper, like summer and barbeques,

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:14.349
and like bacon and…well… bacon goes with
everything. But sometimes you get crime without

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:19.609
punishment and society feels like it’s been
hard done by. We all love a good bit of justice

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:25.009
and there’s nothing quite like a great detective
unravelling a criminal’s evil scheme, although

00:00:25.009 --> 00:00:31.800
it’s not always possible; a vital clue is
missing, witnesses disappear or a bloody fingerprint

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.420
turns out to be ketchup from a hungry detective’s
lunch.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:41.100
So let’s get together Sherlock Holmes, Poirot,
Columbo and that guy from CSI Miami who was

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:51.450
always taking off his sunglasses, and investigate
some of the world’s greatest unsolved crimes.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:56.570
Elizabeth Short was a lot shorter when they
found her since somebody had cut her right

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:03.530
in half. She remains one of Los Angeles longest
unsolved cases and The Black Dahlia, as she

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:09.289
is commonly known, inspired many a good book,
movie and TV show through the years. The nickname

00:01:09.289 --> 00:01:14.520
is likely linked to the 1946 film The Blue
Dahlia, a crime thriller written by one of

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.399
the greatest detective novelists of all time;
Raymond Chandler.

00:01:18.399 --> 00:01:23.399
Elizabeth had a difficult life before her
ugly death. She grew up in Massachusetts and

00:01:23.399 --> 00:01:28.420
when she was just six years old, her father’s
car was found parked on a bridge and it was

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.990
assumed that he had committed suicide after
losing everything in the 1929 stock market

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:41.030
crash. But a letter arrived from California,
years later, with her father apologising and

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:46.439
telling her he lived in California. He couldn’t
find the “sorry I faked my death and ran

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:51.359
away” apology card at the gas station.
Elizabeth eventually moved to join her father

00:01:51.359 --> 00:01:56.189
in California and they lived together in LA
for a while but she moved towns after they

00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:02.029
had an argument and she flitted around various
California locations. Until she was found

00:02:02.029 --> 00:02:07.909
dead in Leimert Park, California.
Right, I guess you want the grizzly details

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:14.780
now, don’t you? Maybe load up a video of
puppies, you know, as back up. So, when Betty

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:20.390
Bersinger and her three-year old daughter
found Elizabeth Short on 15th January 1947,

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:26.940
they thought she was a shop mannequin since
the top and bottom halves of her were over

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:33.330
a foot apart and she was posed with her hands
above her head. She had whole pieces of flesh

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:39.280
removed and was largely drained of blood,
some of which was found in a cement sack nearby.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:45.530
She also had a Glasgow Smile, where the corners
of her mouth were sliced up to her ears.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:50.960
There have been many suspects over the years,
including Walter Bayley, a surgeon; Norman

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:56.500
Chandler, publisher of the Los Angeles Times;
Mark Hansen, a Hollywood nightclub owner and

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:02.540
the most compelling suspect Dr George Hill
Hodel. You can see why they made movies out

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.920
of the story, can’t you?
There are so many rumours about The Black

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.190
Dahlia, such as her being a sex worker, and
even the opposite, that she was unable to

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:16.350
have sex due to a birth defect, none of which
have ever been substantiated.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:24.570
Our next pair of murders involved a whole
lot of beef. But it’s okay vegetarians,

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:30.790
no cows were harmed, just two of the world’s
greatest rappers; Biggie and Tupac.

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:36.150
In 1994, Tupac survived a shooting outside
New York's Quad Studios and he managed to

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.460
get into an elevator and get back upstairs
to where Biggie and some of his crew were.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:45.710
Tupac and Biggie were friends at this point
but Tupac accused Biggie of knowing that the

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:51.520
shooting was going to take place. Biggie denied
it but soon after released the song “Who

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:57.740
Shot Ya?” and, although probably just a
taunt, Tupac took it to heart. Things escalated

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.600
quickly into a full east coast - west coast
rivalry.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.650
Rap beefs are pretty common, and they give
the industry a lot of entertainment value,

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:11.160
often becoming a sort of x-rated soap opera.
But whereas these days, it probably ends with

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:17.720
Azealia Banks being banned from twitter, Tupac
and Biggie had a much more final ending when

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:25.290
both were gunned down, 6 months apart in ‘96
and ’97. No killer has been brought to justice

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:31.040
for either murder, there are just rumours
of various gangsters and even the FBI being

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:35.150
responsible.
Let’s have a break from murder, shall we?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:41.280
No one died for this crime but, it could be
said it actually represented a far more dangerous

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:48.280
threat than everything else on this list.
On Christmas Eve, 2000, a hacker named “Leaf”

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:53.240
accessed a Navy computer in Washington and
stole most of the source code for Exigent's

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:59.460
OS/COMET software, which is used to guide
satellites and missiles. Some geeks have a

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:05.050
very weird idea of what makes a good present;
what is wrong with reindeer print socks?

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:10.570
The FBI’s Chris Murray played down the importance
of the hack, saying it wasn’t an intelligence

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:15.490
disaster since the data was unclassified.
But it’s still pretty worrying that you

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:20.740
could potentially have some thirteen-year-old
kid sitting on classified military information.

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.910
Although, to be fair, we did let George W
Bush have the nuke codes, and he choked on

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:29.930
a pretzel.
Leaf’s identity has never been discovered.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:35.460
The hack was traced back to the University
of Kaiserslautern in Germany but the trail

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.820
went dead.
This is not the only time an unknown hacker

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:45.830
has messed with the US government. In 1989
a digital worm was created, called WANK, which

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:52.070
stood for Worms Against Nuclear Killers. It
infected NASA computers and cost half a million

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:58.120
dollars of time and resources to fix. Computers
infected with the virus were presented with

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:03.210
a message onscreen that said “Your system
has been officially WANKed”. It’s rumoured

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:08.380
that one of the hackers, could have been Wikileaks
founder, Julian Assange.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:15.570
A heist now, one of the biggest unsolved hauls
in history. On February 25th 2005, men disguised

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:20.940
in KLM uniforms, that’s the major Dutch
airline, tricked their way out on to the tarmac

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:26.669
of Amsterdam’s airport, Schiphol. They had
a stolen KLM cargo vehicle and they managed

00:06:26.669 --> 00:06:32.470
to stop an armoured truck which was transporting
uncut diamonds. They took the diamonds at

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:36.480
gun point, although no shots were fired, and
then made off.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:41.240
The truck was found abandoned but the identities
of the robbers remains a mystery. It’s hard

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:45.860
to estimate how much their haul was worth,
since the diamonds were uncut and the cutting

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:51.150
determines a lot of their value. But, it’s
thought to haven been well over $100 million

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:55.880
so that’s not bad for an afternoon’s work.
It’s been noted that this heist bares a

00:06:55.880 --> 00:07:02.550
lot of similarities to the 2013 one in Antwerp,
where men in security uniforms, driving the

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:09.190
vehicles of Belgian security forces, raced
out on to the runway and took 120 boxes full

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:14.830
of diamonds that were being loaded onto a
plane bound for Zurich. In both cases; no

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:20.100
guns were fired, they knew the exact time
and location of the diamonds and the diamonds

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:25.820
were uncut, which also makes them harder to
track. This one was only a haul of a meagre

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:29.520
$50 million though, hardly seems worth the
bother, doesn’t it?

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:35.650
If there is one man you don’t want to mess
with, it’s Vladimir Putin; he runs one of

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:40.290
the world’s most powerful countries, and
he rides a horse without his shirt on, he’s

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:46.169
the manliest of men. But Alexander Litvinenko
decided it would be a good idea to poke the

00:07:46.169 --> 00:07:51.320
angry bear, and, rather than ripping him in
half, the great bear knocked him off with

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:56.460
a sneaky bit of radioactive poisoning. This
is all conjecture, of course.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:01.470
Alexander Litvinenko was a former Russian
FSB officer, who ended up living in London.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:07.280
The Russian FSB are the successors of the
infamous KGB. He left Russia under controversial

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:12.770
circumstances, having been investigated when
he publically accused his superiors of ordering

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:18.790
the assassination of Russian tycoon Boris
Berezovsky. Berezovsky had been a friend of

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:25.030
Putin’s from the early 90s but their relationship
deteriorated soon after Putin left his position

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:29.030
as head of the FSB and became president in
2000.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:35.930
Litvinenko was acquitted twice, in ‘99 and
2000 and subsequently fled to London, where

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:40.990
he worked with British intelligence and wrote
two books, accusing the FSB of some shady

00:08:40.990 --> 00:08:48.130
behaviour which helped Putin claim power.
On 1st November 2006, he fell ill and was

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:54.570
hospitalised, quickly diagnosed as being poisoned
by radioactive polonium-210, which is one

00:08:54.570 --> 00:09:00.430
of the most toxic substances known to mankind.
Obviously, access to the substance is strictly

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:05.180
controlled and there’s also the small fact
that you need access to a nuclear reactor

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:10.670
to actually obtain it. So if you happen to
be at a business meeting with two other Russians

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:16.610
and drink tea containing a lethal dose of
polonium-210, just like Litvinenko did, then

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:19.890
it’s probably no accident. He died on 23rd
November.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:27.120
A British investigation pointed to Andrey
Lugovoy, a Russian government agent, but nothing

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:33.990
could be proven since Russia refused to extradite
him, so the case remains open. The only thing

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:39.100
we know for sure is if a Russian man offers
you a glowing sandwich, politely tell him

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:43.089
you’re not hungry.
Okay, let’s play a quick game of odd one

00:09:43.089 --> 00:09:48.200
out. Which of these sounds like something
you shouldn’t find at the beach; crabs,

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:54.040
sand, seagulls, disembodied human feet, ice
cream. If you said “ice cream”, you had

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:58.500
a very depressing childhood.
Along the coast of the Salish Sea, in British

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:05.140
Columbia, Canada some 20 human feet have been
found on the shore in the last 10 years. Almost

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:10.290
all have been right feet. Also, almost all
of the washed-up feet were wearing running

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:13.480
shoes.
What’s happening then? A serial killer?

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:19.670
Fussy sharks? A really strong ankle high current?
Well, a body can remain in the water for up

00:10:19.670 --> 00:10:25.200
to three decades and feet can easily become
detached through natural decomposition. So

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:30.630
the feet could have just washed up from bodies
of people who have drowned at sea, but why

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:36.620
British Columbia? Nowhere else in the world
have feet washed up on beaches in one location

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:41.540
with such frequency. Does British Columbia
have its very own Dexter-style murderer on

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.390
the loose?
One of the biggest problems in identifying

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:51.060
the source of the lost limbs is that the feet
themselves become difficult to analyse, since

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:54.959
they produce a lot of adipocere. Adipocere
is known as corpse wax and it’s an organic

00:10:54.959 --> 00:11:00.640
substance produced by bacteria during the
decomposition of body fat. It causes difficulties

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:05.910
in forensics because it’s very temperature
dependant so unless you know the exact environment

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:12.020
the body was in during decomposition, it makes
age estimation very difficult.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:16.740
Some feet are from people believed to have
committed suicide. There’s was also a case

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:22.100
of a missing fisherman in the area. It’s
been suggested that some could have come from

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:28.250
the 2004 Asian tsunami, which would match
some of the running shoe’s production locations

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:34.029
and the direction of the currents. Or perhaps
it’s all the work of a serial killer who

00:11:34.029 --> 00:11:38.560
has a grave dislike for those blasted runners
who keep treading up his front yard every

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:43.760
morning. He did warn them!
There’s a surprisingly large crime industry

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.940
around our next topic; after drugs, money
laundering and arms dealing, it’s one of

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:55.610
the biggest illegal businesses in the game.
What do you think it is? Carjacking? Armed

00:11:55.610 --> 00:12:00.910
Robbery? Really awful parking?
It’s actually, the romantic world of art

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:07.470
theft, which clocks in at about $6 billion
annually. And the greatest art heist of all

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:14.149
time was from The Isabella Stewart Gardner
Museum, in Boston, USA. In the early hours

00:12:14.149 --> 00:12:19.410
of 18th March 1990, two men dressed as local
police arrived at the museum and told the

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:24.019
security they’d been called for a disturbance
in the yard. They then proceeded to truss

00:12:24.019 --> 00:12:28.950
up the guards and walked off with an incredible
collection of work from master painters such

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:34.399
as Degas, Rembrandt and Manet. It’s hard
to put a price on it but some say it was almost

00:12:34.399 --> 00:12:40.640
half a billion dollars of classic art. There
were no real leads and none of the art has

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:43.420
resurfaced.
The museum director Anne Hawley saw the bigger

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:49.120
picture and went as far as to release details
for the thieves as to how best to store the

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:53.610
paintings, thinking it’s better that they
at least survive intact, even if they are

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.730
hanging in some shady billionaire’s pool
room.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:13:02.399
It seems like it’s surprisingly easy to
pick up a Picasso or steal a Schiele. In 2010,

00:13:02.399 --> 00:13:08.230
a lone thief just broke a window and cut a
padlock, and that’s all it took to get into

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:14.620
the Paris Museum of Modern Art and dance off
with a Matisse and a Picasso, among others.

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:20.510
Not exactly what I would call state-of-the-art
security. But rather than cashing in on his

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:25.430
millions, one of his accomplices claimed,
while being questioned by the police, that

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:29.519
he had panicked and just thrown the paintings
into a rubbish truck, rather than paint himself

00:13:29.519 --> 00:13:33.350
into a corner and have a nasty brush with
the law.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:39.010
We’re staying with art for our last crime
but now, rather than stealing, the creating

00:13:39.010 --> 00:13:42.470
is the crime.
It’s the world’s favourite graffiti artist,

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.920
the mysterious Banksy. He’s a British artist
that grew out of the underground scene in

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:52.339
Bristol and his work, often highly political
in nature, has appeared everywhere from London

00:13:52.339 --> 00:13:58.399
to Disneyland to the Gaza strip. Pieces of
his work have sold for over $1 million and

00:13:58.399 --> 00:14:02.490
he’s even made an Oscar nominated documentary
called Exit Through The Gift Shop.

00:14:02.490 --> 00:14:08.459
But he, or she or them, has never revealed
their true identity, perhaps to enjoy the

00:14:08.459 --> 00:14:14.589
anonymity but probably due to the illegality
of his work. It’s not just graffiti since

00:14:14.589 --> 00:14:19.279
he’s also done things like produce fake
British bank notes with Princess Dianna replacing

00:14:19.279 --> 00:14:24.660
the Queen and “Banksy of England” written
on them. He also messed with Paris Hilton’s

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:30.490
album launch in 2006 by switching out her
CDs and replacing them with his own remixed

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:36.490
version, including tracks like Why am I Famous?,
What Have I Done? and What Am I For?

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:43.040
A UK newspaper The Mail on Sunday claims to
have proven that Banksy is actually a man

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:49.209
called Robin Gunningham, using geographic
profiling to match his locations and his activity,

00:14:49.209 --> 00:14:54.940
a process normally reserved for serious crime
and tracking viral outbreaks. So maybe the

00:14:54.940 --> 00:15:00.630
writing is on the wall for his anonymity but,
until he’s caught red handed, the mystery

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:04.880
of this world-famous criminal-slash-artist
will remain.

